  "notes": "Four bullets, and bullet 3 is the whole judgement call: 'Complete the quests When the Bow Breaks and Fist of the People' is the header's Quest Reqs field repeated verbatim, even though the walkthrough sequences it BETWEEN the two interviews and the return. A precondition is never a ladder position, so the rung is kept for auditability but flagged optional; it is also unmarkable and unobservable, since no packet reports another quest's completion. gates.prev holds only the header's Previous field (Saga of the Skyserpent) so the quest is not hidden behind quests the page sequences mid-walkthrough. Bullet 2 sends you to two adjutants in Al Zahbi with no order stated, so Gaweesh and Talhaal share a group and both draw at once rather than a strict ladder marking Gaweesh alone. Biyaada's letter is not named as a hand-over, but bullet 2 presupposes you already hold it and the opening cutscene is the only thing that has happened, so it is step 1's evidence; the interview steps only require holding it. Medium overall because of the bullet-3 call.",
